    "interpretation": "The mean band-limited clock of one region correlates with the mean of another region, decaying with inter-region separation at a Gaussian length of ~2,000-3,000 km -- the TEP scale (Steps 53, 58) -- not separation-independent (which a datum / time-scale common mode would give). It survives on precise products, where the satellite-clock common mode is already removed. The network-mean 'common mode' is therefore substantially the TEP field itself: the operational skill measured against persistence / predict-zero (Steps 55, 58) is the TEP contribution, and the skill measured against a bulk mean is a lower bound that removes most of the field."
